      "created_at": "2016-09-15T13:52:20.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Encountered this recently and discussion occurred.</p><p>Guise used I Can Do That, Too to copy Depserate Prey. He&nbsp;played a card and became a crocodile because rawr.</p><p>On the Naturalist's turn, who was also a Crocodile, he played Feral Fury.</p><p>Naturalist applied both effects, then it was Guise's turn. However, the effects on the card reference the Naturalist explicitly as the source of the damage. As Desperate Prey doesn't mention the hero, we ruled that the Naturalist&nbsp;did the damage as there was nothing to override it.</p><p>This later also allowed Guise to&nbsp;troll the Naturalist with Indomitable Force.</p><p>What are other people's views of this interaction?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:48:06.898Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
