      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-09-16T12:09:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"pwatson1974\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/48/1925_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> pwatson1974:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Except Desperate Prey says \"Until the end of your next turn, you may activate that icon's effects.\" It doesn't say anything about the card you activate having to be yours. In the same way ICDTT can copy the Arent Adept and activate a performance even if Guise hasn't copied any. Why would this be different?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I'd play it this way as well Pwatson. I'm more inclined toward your argument.</p>",
